        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(restart-sentinel): log DB errors instead of silently swallowing them",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n`clearRestartSentinel`, `readRestartSentinel`, and `hasRestartSentinel` used empty `catch {}` / `catch { return null }` / `catch { return false }` blocks that silently swallowed SQLite DB errors. This PR replaces them with `sentinelLog.warn(...)` so errors are visible in diagnostics while preserving the best-effort semantics.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nIn `src/infra/restart-sentinel.ts`, three exported functions silently discard all errors from the SQLite state database:\n\n- **`clearRestartSentinel`** — `catch {}`: If the DB write fails (locked, corrupt, disk full), the sentinel is not cleared but the caller has no way to detect this. The gateway may continue to believe a restart is pending.\n- **`readRestartSentinel`** — `catch { return null }`: Any DB read error (transient lock, corruption) is treated identically to \"no sentinel exists\", potentially causing a pending restart to be silently dropped.\n- **`hasRestartSentinel`** — `catch { return false }`: Same problem — DB errors are indistinguishable from \"no sentinel\".\n\n**Code evidence**: In `restart-sentinel.ts:228`, the `catch {}` on the `runOpenClawStateWriteTransaction` call provides no visibility into whether the sentinel was actually cleared.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe functions were written with best-effort semantics (they must not throw during shutdown/cleanup), but the empty catch blocks went too far by discarding all diagnostic information. Unlike the intentional best-effort pattern in `ensureOpenClawStatePermissions` (which includes a comment explaining why the catch is empty), these catch blocks had no explanation and no logging.\n\n## Why This Fix\n\nFollows the same pattern accepted in:\n- [#84449](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/84449) (`fix(delivery): log failDelivery errors instead of silently swallowing`) by @SebTardif\n- [#82943](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/82943) (`fix(agents): log warnings instead of swallowing subagent errors`) by @SebTardif\n\nUses `createSubsystemLogger(\"restart-sentinel\")` + `formatErrorMessage(err)` — consistent with `restart.ts` which also uses `createSubsystemLogger(\"restart\")`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- **Before**: Operators had no diagnostic signal when the restart sentinel could not be cleared or read — failures were completely invisible.\n- **After**: A warning is emitted to the diagnostics log (`[restart-sentinel]` prefix) with the full error context, while the functions continue to return safe defaults (`null` / `false` / `undefined`).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before**: No warnings emitted on stderr when the DB operation fails — errors are silently swallowed.\n- **After**: Three warnings emitted with full error context; functions return safely without throwing.\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Before (on main, `catch {}`)\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx scripts/proof-restart-sentinel-catch.mjs\n=== clearRestartSentinel ===\nclearRestartSentinel completed without throwing\n\n=== readRestartSentinel ===\nreadRestartSentinel returned: null\n\n=== hasRestartSentinel ===\nhasRestartSentinel returned: false\n\n=== stderr (warnings captured) ===\nFAIL: No warnings were emitted on stderr!\n      The catch blocks are silently swallowing errors.\n```\n\n### After (with fix)\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx scripts/proof-restart-sentinel-catch.mjs\n=== clearRestartSentinel ===\nclearRestartSentinel completed without throwing\n\n=== readRestartSentinel ===\nreadRestartSentinel returned: null\n\n=== hasRestartSentinel ===\nhasRestartSentinel returned: false\n\n=== stderr (warnings captured) ===\nPASS: Warnings were emitted on stderr:\n  [restart-sentinel] Failed to clear restart sentinel: ...\n  [restart-sentinel] Failed to read restart sentinel: ...\n  [restart-sentinel] Failed to check restart sentinel: ...\n```\n\n## Tests and Validation\n\n- `pnpm check` passed (no lint errors)\n- Added 3 regression tests in `restart-sentinel.test.ts` verifying that each function survives DB failures without throwing and returns the safe default value\n",
